{
  "reference_answer": "Teamwork is useful mainly because it lets people cover each other's weak spots. Nobody is good at everything, so when you work with others, you can lean on their strengths and they can lean on yours. I remember doing a group project where I was fine with research but terrible at presenting. One of my teammates was the opposite, and honestly, the final result was way better than anything I could have done alone. It also speeds things up, because you can split tasks and get feedback early instead of going down the wrong path. And on top of that, working in a team teaches you how to deal with different personalities, which is a skill you need pretty much everywhere. So it's not just about getting the job done faster — it's also about learning from each other along the way.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：团队合作的价值在于互补短板、加速反馈并锻炼人际协作；示例为虚构，不代表用户经历。",
